WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.899
In Emperor Wu's time, the Xiongnu repeatedly came south, harassing the northern frontier.

00:00:06.399 --> 00:00:14.174
Emperor Wu resolved to appoint Wei Qing and Huo Qubing as generals to lead the counterattack.

00:00:14.674 --> 00:00:22.288
The Han cavalry assembled and set out, warhorses neighing and banners flying in the wind.

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:34.081
Huo Qubing, barely in his twenties, was brave and resourceful, leading elite cavalry deep into the steppe to raid the Xiongnu camp.

00:00:34.581 --> 00:00:43.976
The steady Wei Qing led the main army, arraying his formations and advancing step by step.

00:00:44.476 --> 00:00:54.794
After several great battles, the Han army won a complete victory, and Han's banners were planted on the northern steppe.

00:00:55.294 --> 00:01:05.075
But the long war also made the country pay an enormous price in wealth and manpower.

